1
00:00:00,620 --> 00:00:03,420
It seems Japan is changing their formation.

2
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:06,500
They're bringing on Misugi-kun in place of Nitta-kun.

3
00:00:08,510 --> 00:00:09,720
Misugi.

4
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:13,140
Not as a player, but as a coach.

5
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:14,050
A coach?

6
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:17,220
We know you're an incredibly talented player.

7
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,230
But you also have a heart condition.

8
00:00:22,190 --> 00:00:26,270
Despite that, you're not just a unique footballer,

9
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:29,360
you also have the ability to calmly analyze those around you.

10
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:33,320
We want you to use these good skills to guide the team as a coach.

11
00:00:33,410 --> 00:00:35,660
And to strengthen them by working on their weak points.

12
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:37,540
Misugi-kun.

13
00:00:37,830 --> 00:00:40,080
I never give up on my dream of wearing the national team jersey

14
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:42,960
and being on the field.

15
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:44,710
Misugi.

16
00:00:45,290 --> 00:00:46,670
Misugi?

17
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,050
He's been the team's trainer until now.

18
00:00:50,130 --> 00:00:52,510
But I registered him as a player for this tournament.

19
00:00:52,590 --> 00:00:54,640
Guys, I trust all of you.

20
00:00:55,010 --> 00:00:58,640
The glass baby, the field's nobleman, Jun Misugi.

21
00:00:58,850 --> 00:01:02,140
Could he be Japan's secret weapon?

22
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:04,940
He was with the team as a coach.

23
00:01:05,020 --> 00:01:10,490
But Misugi-kun hasn't played at all since the Japan team arrived for the European tournament and this tournament.

24
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:14,030
But in this match against Argentina, for the first time, he's on the field.

25
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:29,670
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

26
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:47,520
Tokyo

27
00:02:47,850 --> 00:02:51,980
Episode 17: The Field's Nobleman Returns!!

28
00:02:50,390 --> 00:02:51,980
Welcome home, dear.

29
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:55,480
Is Jun really playing in the match?

30
00:02:55,650 --> 00:02:58,030
Yes, he just entered the game.

31
00:02:58,110 --> 00:02:59,860
Oh, that's wonderful.

32
00:03:02,990 --> 00:03:03,820
Jun.

33
00:03:04,830 --> 00:03:07,910
Mr. Director, how are things?

34
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,540
I'm fine.

35
00:03:09,750 --> 00:03:14,460
I accompanied the team in Europe as a coach.

36
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:18,840
Of course, being in the cradle of football taught me a lot.

37
00:03:19,590 --> 00:03:23,930
Until now, I was watching the Japan team's matches from the bench.

38
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:27,560
But I don't intend to stay as a football coach.

39
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:32,270
At the first opportunity, I'll step onto the field.

40
00:03:34,860 --> 00:03:36,360
I trust you, Misugi-san.

41
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:39,360
Okay, leave it to me, Nitta.

42
00:03:41,610 --> 00:03:43,780
With Misugi-kun's arrival,

43
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:48,870
will Japan youth be able to break this deadlock?

44
00:03:49,950 --> 00:03:51,500
We trust you, Misugi.

45
00:03:51,790 --> 00:03:55,750
Throughout our matches, you were a coach.

46
00:03:55,830 --> 00:03:59,880
But I know that in your heart, you experienced them as if you were playing yourself.

47
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:05,180
Jun Misugi, everyone on the team knows how talented you are.

48
00:04:05,550 --> 00:04:12,230
Use this coaching experience and pave the way to victory.

49
00:04:13,850 --> 00:04:16,310
Three years have passed, hasn't it, Tsubasa-kun?

50
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:22,030
As I promised, I'm finally standing on the field next to you.

51
00:04:23,650 --> 00:04:26,780
Yes, I remember well, Misugi-kun.

52
00:04:27,370 --> 00:04:30,370
Nice to see you, I'm Misugi from Musashi.

53
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:33,410
And I'm Ozora Tsubasa, pleased to meet you.

54
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:36,170
I'm looking forward to our match.

55
00:04:36,250 --> 00:04:43,510
Musashi Team

56
00:04:36,670 --> 00:04:39,920
The Musashi team is the strongest team in the Kanto region.

57
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,510
Its main squad consists of elites selected from over 1000 candidates.

58
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:49,140
What really sets them apart is their star and captain, Jun Misugi.

59
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:51,970
His technique is far superior to that of an ordinary elementary school student.

60
00:04:52,060 --> 00:04:54,480
And with his elegant playing style,

61
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:56,480
he doesn't allow the opponent to make physical contact.

62
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:59,820
That's why he's been nicknamed the field's nobleman, right coach?

63
00:04:59,900 --> 00:04:59,900

64
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:00,900
Understood.

65
00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:05,240
Yes, but he hasn't played at all in this tournament.

66
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:06,910
Was he injured?

67
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:09,120
Well, no one knows the reason.

68
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:12,700
But Misugi is famous for rarely playing.

69
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:16,000
Tsubasa-kun, Tsubasa-kun, please.

70
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:18,040
Let our captain win.

71
00:05:18,290 --> 00:05:21,840
Actually, our captain has a weak heart and can't play football anymore.

72
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:26,590
Can't play football?

73
00:05:27,050 --> 00:05:29,800
His doctor told him not to play.

74
00:05:29,890 --> 00:05:32,970
But he insists on playing until the end of this tournament.

75
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:35,100
So that's why he wasn't playing.

76
00:05:35,430 --> 00:05:38,900
Only me and the coach know about this.

77
00:05:39,230 --> 00:05:41,360
Welcome to the second half of the semifinal match.

78
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:43,530
Nankatsu team against Musashi team.

79
00:05:43,940 --> 00:05:46,780
We see the players of both teams entering the field.

80
00:05:49,740 --> 00:05:51,030
Misugi-kun!

81
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:52,790
Jun-kun!

82
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:56,540
I shouldn't wait for the ball to come to me.

83
00:05:56,750 --> 00:05:57,620
Then...

84
00:05:59,670 --> 00:06:04,050
What's this? Misugi-kun isn't passing and is waiting for Tsubasa-kun.

85
00:06:04,250 --> 00:06:05,170
Tsubasa-kun.

86
00:06:05,340 --> 00:06:08,550
Does he have that much confidence in his ball keeping?

87
00:06:08,630 --> 00:06:13,810
Tsubasa-kun, I've been waiting for this moment, this is our one-on-one battle.

88
00:06:14,140 --> 00:06:16,480
The ball is mine.

89
00:06:17,350 --> 00:06:19,850
He strikes hard with his elbow.

90
00:06:25,030 --> 00:06:26,030
Misugi-kun.

91
00:06:26,110 --> 00:06:27,610
Tsubasa-kun, come quickly!

92
00:06:28,530 --> 00:06:29,610
Okay.

93
00:06:30,610 --> 00:06:33,910
What's this? Tsubasa-kun blocked his path.

94
00:06:33,990 --> 00:06:36,500
This will be their second confrontation.

95
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:40,870
Tsubasa-kun, do you know about my heart?

96
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:41,920
What?

97
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:45,340
So you do know, Tsubasa-kun.

98
00:06:45,420 --> 00:06:48,090
Oh, the ball is going toward Misugi-kun.

99
00:06:49,430 --> 00:06:54,560
Tsubasa-kun, I'll show you, you're not the only one who can do this.

100
00:06:58,140 --> 00:06:59,480
No, he...

101
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:01,270
U-Unbelievable.

102
00:07:01,730 --> 00:07:02,650
He did it!

103
00:07:02,730 --> 00:07:05,400
Now Misugi-kun executes a return shot.

104
00:07:09,860 --> 00:07:11,860
What an incredible shot!

105
00:07:13,030 --> 00:07:15,660
Musashi takes the lead once again.

106
00:07:17,830 --> 00:07:22,420
Musashi, no, Misugi-kun has now completely taken control of the game.

107
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:23,920
I'll do it.

108
00:07:25,790 --> 00:07:28,880
I'll make up for these two goals.

109
00:07:29,090 --> 00:07:31,760
Incredible! Tsubasa-kun uses the wetness of the ground to do a flip.

110
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:33,890
His flip speed is greater than the run of Musashi's players.

111
00:07:34,090 --> 00:07:34,930
What?

112
00:07:35,010 --> 00:07:36,010
And what's this?

113
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:38,310
He's preparing to shoot with a flip.

114
00:07:41,060 --> 00:07:42,980
Goal! Equalizer!

115
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:47,730
Tsubasa-kun shot with a flip using the wetness of the ground.

116
00:07:46,110 --> 00:07:47,730
6th National Cup Tournament
Second Semifinal Match

117
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:49,740
We finally equalized.

118
00:07:49,990 --> 00:07:51,450
You did it, Tsubasa-kun.

119
00:07:51,530 --> 00:07:53,740
It seems the rainy ground is also your friend.

120
00:07:56,870 --> 00:07:59,290
What's this?

121
00:07:59,830 --> 00:08:01,910
The Musashi team captain Misugi-kun,

122
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,880
has fallen to the ground and is clutching his chest.

123
00:08:05,170 --> 00:08:06,000
Misugi-kun.

124
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:08,800
Tsubasa-kun cleared the ball.

125
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:11,010
But Misugi-kun also blocked him.

126
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:17,100
Incredible! The ball goes over their heads!

127
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:21,520
My eyes.

128
00:08:21,930 --> 00:08:23,810
I cleared it, I cleared it.

129
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:28,980
The ball... my ball...

130
00:08:29,610 --> 00:08:31,940
Ball, where's the ball?

131
00:08:32,610 --> 00:08:35,030
Where did the ball go?

132
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:39,080
Captain! The ball is right above your head!

133
00:08:40,490 --> 00:08:42,830
I can see it, I can see it.

134
00:08:43,080 --> 00:08:44,500
My ball.

135
00:08:47,170 --> 00:08:48,130
Right here.

136
00:08:48,210 --> 00:08:50,300
Misugi-kun's shot is a moment faster.

137
00:08:51,420 --> 00:08:53,130
Morizaki-kun can't catch it.

138
00:08:53,220 --> 00:08:54,170
He scored!

139
00:08:54,260 --> 00:08:57,050
Misugi-kun scores with determination.

140
00:08:57,180 --> 00:08:58,800
Get ready, Misugi-kun!

141
00:09:05,140 --> 00:09:08,360
Tsubasa-kun makes an incredible long-distance shot.

142
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:12,070
Come on! The ball goes even faster on the wet ground.

143
00:09:12,230 --> 00:09:14,900
This type of shot is a nightmare for any goalkeeper.

144
00:09:14,990 --> 00:09:17,490
No, Tawaza-kun can't reach it.

145
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:19,660
But Misugi-kun comes.

146
00:09:22,450 --> 00:09:24,910
Misugi-kun, just one step short of reaching it.

147
00:09:27,210 --> 00:09:28,170
Tsubasa-kun.

148
00:09:29,460 --> 00:09:32,000
I'm not giving up on football.

149
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:40,300
Even if I can only play 1 or 2 minutes, I swear I'll step onto the field.

150
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:44,560
And one day, I will overcome this heart disease.

151
00:09:44,980 --> 00:09:46,230
Misugi-kun.

152
00:09:47,440 --> 00:09:51,900
When you recover, we'll fight together once again.

153
00:09:52,230 --> 00:09:53,940
That's what you promised me, right?

154
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:55,150
Yes.

155
00:09:55,570 --> 00:10:00,320
Though now we're both playing for the Japan team.

156
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:06,500
Guys, I know you're all tired in these final minutes.

157
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:09,170
But let's focus on these last 5 minutes.

158
00:10:09,250 --> 00:10:12,670
If we can do this, I know we'll find a way to win.

159
00:10:13,090 --> 00:10:13,920
Okay!

160
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:17,800
Argentina may be strong, but we've regained our morale.

161
00:10:18,180 --> 00:10:19,840
Right.

162
00:10:22,140 --> 00:10:25,180
We return to the moment of Argentina's throw-in.

163
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:32,190
Argentina wants to give the ball to Diaz, but Tsubasa-kun is marking him tightly.

164
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:34,730
Number 10 is marking Diaz.

165
00:10:34,940 --> 00:10:35,940
In this situation...

166
00:10:37,110 --> 00:10:40,450
Oh, Pascal-kun starts dribbling alone.

167
00:10:40,700 --> 00:10:42,450
Good, come on, Pascal.

168
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:44,950
- Good, I'm going.
- Misugi.

169
00:10:45,620 --> 00:10:49,710
Misugi-kun, who just joined the Japan team, goes to stop him.

170
00:10:49,870 --> 00:10:51,210
A breakthrough path.

171
00:10:51,460 --> 00:10:55,880
This kid just came on, so he can't match my speed.

172
00:10:56,210 --> 00:10:57,210
Right here!

173
00:10:57,380 --> 00:10:59,090
- Great!
- You got past him, Pascal.

174
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:01,590
He got past Misugi-kun.

175
00:11:02,470 --> 00:11:03,720
What?

176
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:04,680
Pascal.

177
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:05,890
Great, Misugi.

178
00:11:06,220 --> 00:11:10,140
He deliberately left a breakthrough path to deceive Pascal.

179
00:11:10,230 --> 00:11:13,650
Alright, let's go guys, time for a quick breakaway.

180
00:11:13,730 --> 00:11:14,820
Okay!

181
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:17,610
The Japan team won the ball back.

182
00:11:17,690 --> 00:11:19,650
Time to counterattack.

183
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:21,660
Very well done, Misugi.

184
00:11:22,160 --> 00:11:24,160
During the Elementary School National Cup,

185
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:28,410
you stunned Tsubasa and the rest of us with your incredible plays.

186
00:11:28,870 --> 00:11:30,620
Misugi-kun stops him.

187
00:11:30,710 --> 00:11:32,540
Nankatsu can't score the first goal.

188
00:11:35,630 --> 00:11:37,340
Let's do this, Tsubasa-kun.

189
00:11:37,630 --> 00:11:38,460
Okay.

190
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:41,590
Oh, Tsubasa-kun caught up with him.

191
00:11:43,890 --> 00:11:46,850
But Misugi-kun leaped out of his path.

192
00:11:46,930 --> 00:11:49,480
Let's go forward guys, follow Misugi!

193
00:11:49,810 --> 00:11:52,310
I may have just entered the game,

194
00:11:52,390 --> 00:11:56,480
but I've been playing this match from the bench since it began.

195
00:11:56,770 --> 00:12:00,240
I've studied all of Argentina's movements.

196
00:12:00,610 --> 00:12:05,950
Defensive midfielder Ruggeri, fast, but slow to react from the sides.

197
00:12:07,870 --> 00:12:09,870
Right midfielder, Palos.

198
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:13,040
A functional player with great defense and offense.

199
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:15,330
But his stamina drained toward the end of the match.

200
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:16,340
What?

201
00:12:16,420 --> 00:12:17,250
Damn it.

202
00:12:17,340 --> 00:12:19,170
Left midfielder, Jettis.

203
00:12:19,250 --> 00:12:21,220
A midfield support pillar due to his height.

204
00:12:21,300 --> 00:12:25,510
Great in aerial balls, but that makes his feet weak.

205
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:29,930
Oh, Misugi-kun passes his opponents one by one.

206
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:32,850
He's approaching Argentina's goal.

207
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:35,730
This kid...

208
00:12:36,110 --> 00:12:36,940
Damn it.

209
00:12:37,020 --> 00:12:38,690
Defense, Sembro.

210
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:41,190
His technique and attacks are strong, but...

211
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:44,950
He can't hit me.

212
00:12:45,360 --> 00:12:46,200
What?

213
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:50,160
Floats like a butterfly, stings like a bee. What incredible play!

214
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:53,710
This is the playing style of the field's nobleman, Jun Misugi.

215
00:12:51,750 --> 00:12:53,750
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

216
00:12:57,770 --> 00:12:59,980
Born: June 23, Height: 169 cm, Weight: 57 kg, Blood Type: A

217
00:13:00,270 --> 00:13:04,190
This is the playing style of the field's nobleman, Jun Misugi.

218
00:13:06,740 --> 00:13:08,910
What incredible technique.

219
00:13:08,990 --> 00:13:10,990
I didn't think there was someone like him in Japan.

220
00:13:11,330 --> 00:13:14,500
Those incredible dribbles are just like Pierre.

221
00:13:15,080 --> 00:13:16,500
Who is this kid?

222
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:19,500
Like it was just yesterday, Misugi-kun.

223
00:13:20,210 --> 00:13:22,750
That rainy semifinal in Japan.

224
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:28,050
You were already a midfielder, just like Tsubasa-kun is now.

225
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:32,930
Tsubasa-kun is going to goal and is completely unmarked.

226
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:36,850
Tsubasa-kun.

227
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:39,940
Will Misaki-kun's pass reach him?

228
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:41,400
He did it.

229
00:13:41,940 --> 00:13:44,480
Tsubasa-kun is completely free in front of the goal.

230
00:13:44,730 --> 00:13:46,320
Get him.

231
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:48,700
He managed to score!

232
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:49,700
Great.

233
00:13:49,780 --> 00:13:52,320
Nankatsu turns the score around.

234
00:13:52,410 --> 00:13:54,200
This is incredible.

235
00:13:55,620 --> 00:13:59,040
What happened? The linesman raised his flag.

236
00:13:59,710 --> 00:14:01,460
Offside was called.

237
00:14:01,540 --> 00:14:02,960
- What?
- Offside?

238
00:14:04,630 --> 00:14:09,010
Incredible, is Musashi a master of the offside tactic?

239
00:14:09,630 --> 00:14:14,930
Even back in elementary school, you controlled the game as you wished.

240
00:14:15,010 --> 00:14:17,020
Your football talent is truly limitless.

241
00:14:17,310 --> 00:14:19,230
Stop him! Stop that guy!

242
00:14:19,310 --> 00:14:22,020
Misugi-kun just entered the game.

243
00:14:22,310 --> 00:14:23,940
Japan team's trump card.

244
00:14:24,020 --> 00:14:28,320
Using his unique talent, he's tearing Argentina's territory apart.

245
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:29,530
Jun.

246
00:14:30,110 --> 00:14:33,780
Jun, his whole life he's fought against heart disease.

247
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:39,410
That's why he could never play full matches from the very beginning.

248
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:41,790
And that's why he sometimes had tough times.

249
00:14:41,870 --> 00:14:45,960
But he'd been getting physiotherapy since elementary school.

250
00:14:45,130 --> 00:14:47,880
Oizumi General Hospital

251
00:14:46,250 --> 00:14:47,880
Good, I approve.

252
00:14:48,460 --> 00:14:50,550
R-Really?

253
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:54,890
You mean, I can play football again?

254
00:14:55,350 --> 00:14:59,310
Your determination and hard work for football left me no choice.

255
00:14:59,390 --> 00:15:01,140
I allow you to enter the tournament.

256
00:15:02,140 --> 00:15:03,900
Hooray! I did it!

257
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:06,480
Congratulations, captain.

258
00:15:06,820 --> 00:15:08,230
Director.

259
00:15:08,820 --> 00:15:12,860
Thank you for taking care of everything these two years.

260
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:15,740
Thanks to you, I can play in one more match.

261
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:19,870
Oh, I'm sorry.

262
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:21,250
It's fine.

263
00:15:22,040 --> 00:15:26,500
You were able to play again in your third year.

264
00:15:29,210 --> 00:15:31,170
The whistle signals the end of the match.

265
00:15:32,090 --> 00:15:33,180
Toho Academy.

266
00:15:33,260 --> 00:15:36,260
Going to the National Cup for the third consecutive time.

267
00:15:40,390 --> 00:15:41,230
Good.

268
00:15:43,730 --> 00:15:45,650
We came so close, didn't we, Misugi?

269
00:15:45,810 --> 00:15:46,650
Yes.

270
00:15:47,940 --> 00:15:52,440
I couldn't play against Tsubasa-kun again after three years, but...

271
00:15:53,450 --> 00:15:57,200
You couldn't make it to the National Cup, but...

272
00:15:57,370 --> 00:15:58,450
I know.

273
00:15:58,990 --> 00:16:05,000
Even after being selected as a coach for the Japan team, you continued your training.

274
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:09,590
That's why you can overcome it, Jun.

275
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:11,460
I won't let you go any further.

276
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:14,720
Misugi-kun passes.

277
00:16:15,180 --> 00:16:16,550
The ball goes toward Tsubasa-kun.

278
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:18,930
Diaz-kun comes from behind Tsubasa-kun.

279
00:16:19,010 --> 00:16:20,430
Catch, Misugi-kun.

280
00:16:20,720 --> 00:16:22,980
He immediately returns the ball to Misugi-kun.

281
00:16:23,060 --> 00:16:23,930
Misaki-kun.

282
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:26,690
Misugi-kun now passes to Misaki-kun.

283
00:16:26,770 --> 00:16:28,690
- I'll cut you off.
- Catch, Misugi-kun.

284
00:16:28,980 --> 00:16:31,570
Misugi-kun, who just entered the field,

285
00:16:31,650 --> 00:16:34,110
is making wonderful passes with Tsubasa-kun and Misaki-kun.

286
00:16:34,190 --> 00:16:35,450
Catch, Hyuga.

287
00:16:35,780 --> 00:16:38,700
Misugi-kun passes to Hyuga-kun in front of the goal.

288
00:16:39,370 --> 00:16:40,580
Misugi.

289
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:44,290
The Tokyo preliminary final to go to this year's National Cup...

290
00:16:44,830 --> 00:16:48,750
We're in the 22nd minute of the first half and Misugi-kun enters the field.

291
00:16:49,210 --> 00:16:55,970
Damned glass baby, with your dazzling technique, you almost finished me.

292
00:16:56,050 --> 00:16:57,430
- Now.
- What?

293
00:16:58,640 --> 00:17:02,310
I'll get past all of you with fast dribbling.

294
00:17:02,390 --> 00:17:03,430
Now.

295
00:17:04,310 --> 00:17:07,310
Misugi-kun takes the ball with a side tackle.

296
00:17:08,100 --> 00:17:10,150
Football isn't an individual sport.

297
00:17:10,230 --> 00:17:12,400
Team play is also important, Hyuga.

298
00:17:12,480 --> 00:17:13,650
Damn bastard.

299
00:17:14,150 --> 00:17:16,650
I won't lose at this stage.

300
00:17:17,950 --> 00:17:18,780
What?

301
00:17:19,160 --> 00:17:20,660
What a surprise.

302
00:17:20,740 --> 00:17:22,790
He breaks free from the defenders, but still doesn't pass.

303
00:17:22,950 --> 00:17:25,040
He heads directly and alone toward the goal.

304
00:17:25,160 --> 00:17:26,790
No, he outplayed us.

305
00:17:30,670 --> 00:17:33,460
Goal! Score 3-1!

306
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:35,260
Damn it.

307
00:17:35,340 --> 00:17:36,840
I can't get away from him.

308
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:38,840
What's going on here? I have to get past!

309
00:17:40,300 --> 00:17:41,140
Cut him...

310
00:17:44,930 --> 00:17:45,770
Misugi.

311
00:17:45,850 --> 00:17:46,810
Captain.

312
00:17:46,890 --> 00:17:47,730
Misugi.

313
00:17:47,810 --> 00:17:48,850
Misugi.

314
00:17:48,940 --> 00:17:51,400
Oh, what happened to Misugi-kun!?

315
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:54,320
He suddenly collapsed on Hyuga and falls to the ground.

316
00:17:55,820 --> 00:17:57,110
Guys...

317
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:01,120
What?

318
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:08,790
Playing with you, things got out of control.

319
00:18:08,870 --> 00:18:11,670
I realized I'd gotten too soft.

320
00:18:13,420 --> 00:18:14,800
Coach Kira.

321
00:18:15,670 --> 00:18:16,880
A championship flag?

322
00:18:17,630 --> 00:18:20,720
It seems you're proud of yourself, aren't you?

323
00:18:22,300 --> 00:18:26,270
Right now, you're a toothless tiger in a cage.

324
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:31,400
A toothless tiger...?

325
00:18:33,060 --> 00:18:35,230
If I hadn't played that match against you,

326
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:38,440
I would have never gone to Okinawa for that hell training.

327
00:18:39,110 --> 00:18:42,360
And I would have never acquired the Tiger Shot.

328
00:18:42,610 --> 00:18:46,620
Misugi-kun crosses the ball for Hyuga, but Passaro-kun also goes after it.

329
00:18:47,910 --> 00:18:51,750
Jun Misugi, if you didn't have a heart condition,

330
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:56,750
you might have been Japan's best striker.

331
00:18:57,550 --> 00:19:00,260
He passes back to Misugi-kun.

332
00:19:00,630 --> 00:19:03,890
Will Misugi-kun shoot?

333
00:19:03,970 --> 00:19:04,800
Misugi.

334
00:19:04,890 --> 00:19:05,760
Misugi-kun.

335
00:19:06,140 --> 00:19:07,680
I won't allow you.

336
00:19:07,770 --> 00:19:11,270
But Galvan-kun from Argentina goes to block his shot.

337
00:19:13,230 --> 00:19:16,110
Misugi-kun quickly passes.

338
00:19:16,190 --> 00:19:17,820
It goes toward Tsubasa-kun.

339
00:19:17,900 --> 00:19:20,110
Tsubasa-kun approaches it.

340
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:22,450
Your pass was great, Misugi-kun.

341
00:19:22,530 --> 00:19:25,160
Tsubasa-kun was focused on a goal pass.

342
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:27,620
But now he makes a jumping volley.

343
00:19:27,870 --> 00:19:29,370
I'll never let you shoot.

344
00:19:29,790 --> 00:19:32,250
What's this? Diaz-kun reaches once again.

345
00:19:32,330 --> 00:19:34,500
He blocks Tsubasa-kun's shot with a tackle technique.

346
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:37,710
The Japan team couldn't shoot and turn the score around.

347
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:39,880
- Tsubasa.
- This isn't good.

348
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:42,630
What?

349
00:19:43,180 --> 00:19:47,140
Misugi-kun may have predicted that Diaz-kun would block that shot.

350
00:19:47,260 --> 00:19:50,390
Faster than anyone, he jumped for the spinning ball.

351
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:51,640
Misugi-kun!

352
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:53,390
He...

353
00:19:53,770 --> 00:19:54,850
Right.

354
00:19:54,940 --> 00:20:00,400
We know how hard Misugi worked as our coach to support the Japan team.

355
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:03,400
And how extraordinary Misugi-san's current play is.

356
00:20:03,700 --> 00:20:07,160
Likewise, how hard it was for him not being able to be on the field.

357
00:20:07,450 --> 00:20:09,660
Shoot, Misugi!

358
00:20:09,950 --> 00:20:11,120
I'll score.

359
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:14,920
I have to score for the Japan team to win.

360
00:20:15,330 --> 00:20:20,300
For my coach who believed in me, and for everyone giving their all.

361
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:23,800
And most importantly, for myself.

362
00:20:24,050 --> 00:20:25,590
Be a goal!

363
00:20:26,010 --> 00:20:28,680
This is Misugi-kun's fascinating move!

364
00:20:28,850 --> 00:20:30,850
This is a return shot!

365
00:20:37,440 --> 00:20:38,810
He finished it!

366
00:20:38,900 --> 00:20:44,650
Misugi-kun's return shot entered Argentina's goal from the right corner.

367
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:45,740
The score is turned around!

368
00:20:45,820 --> 00:20:49,280
The Japan team takes the lead for the first time in this match.

369
00:20:49,370 --> 00:20:52,160
This goal was vital for them to advance to the top four.

370
00:20:52,660 --> 00:20:54,660
I did it!

371
00:20:54,870 --> 00:20:56,580
You did it, Misugi.

372
00:20:56,670 --> 00:20:59,420
You're truly a genius, Jun Misugi.

373
00:20:59,540 --> 00:21:01,420
Yes! We turned the score around!

374
00:21:01,840 --> 00:21:03,050
Now it's 5-4.

375
00:21:03,130 --> 00:21:04,880
Two minutes left in the match.

376
00:21:04,970 --> 00:21:07,840
Japan youth finally turned the score in their favor.

377
00:21:07,930 --> 00:21:11,390
All of this happened thanks to Misugi-kun, who entered the field in the 25th minute of the second half.

378
00:21:11,470 --> 00:21:14,680
The Japan team made a golden substitution.

379
00:21:17,140 --> 00:21:20,440
What a wonderful return shot that was.

380
00:21:20,560 --> 00:21:22,190
By adding spin to the ball,

381
00:21:22,270 --> 00:21:24,610
the ball went with curve and entered the goal.

382
00:21:24,690 --> 00:21:28,160
Misugi-kun invented this return shot model himself.

383
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:31,780
Japan has another genius, his name is Jun Misugi.

384
00:21:31,870 --> 00:21:35,580
He returned after overcoming his heart disease.

385
00:21:35,660 --> 00:21:39,290
That incredible goal was crucial for the victory.

386
00:21:39,380 --> 00:21:42,340
Jun, it was astonishing, astonishing.

387
00:21:42,750 --> 00:21:47,090
And the one who helped him was the other genius, Tsubasa-kun.

388
00:21:47,170 --> 00:21:50,720
He delivered brilliant passes on all the goals in this match.

389
00:21:51,050 --> 00:21:53,220
After the Italy match,

390
00:21:53,310 --> 00:21:57,180
the Japan team once again put on an unexpected show.

391
00:21:57,520 --> 00:22:00,980
If it happens twice, it's not unexpected.

392
00:22:01,560 --> 00:22:05,400
Without a doubt, we have now witnessed the true power of the Japan team.

393
00:23:46,590 --> 00:24:50,050
NEXT EPISODE: THE TOP FOUR COME TOGETHER!!